Jeremy Matthew Toeman (Shaggy+@CMU.EDU) wrote:
: Occasionally I get a message "You feel wise, you must have been
: observant" and my wisdom goes up. Sometimes my dexterity too, and
: occasionally they drop..  Why does this happen, and can I control it so
: I can increase all my stats?

	The game keeps track of your actions and every now and then
 checks to determine whether you've been exercising or abusing your
 stats. The activities that affect your characteristics are numerous,
 but highly logical -- for example carrying a lot of stuff or pushing
 boulders exercise your strength while suffering from hunger will abuse
 STR.

	Total control over your stats is very hard to accomplish without
 actually knowing all the circumstances that exercise your stats. They
 are listed in the v8.00 spoilers, but you may not want to read them...


: Should you donate money to a priest of a different god than yours?

	Go ahead, if you can afford it. I won't spoil you right away,
 but it doesn't hurt to know that donating gold to a priest of any
 alignment is beneficial.


: If your god gives you several artifact weapons (at altars), can you sell
: the ones you don't want to use, or will that piss him off?

	The latest spoilers from krl say nothing about that really. I
 guess you may sell them. Are they worth a lot?


: How many levels are there in the Gnomish Mines, and what is the overall
: point to them, aside from just gaining much experience?

	It depends -- about a dozen I think. The Mines are worth a
 thorough venture: pick axes, gems, and potions galore, the mine town
 (candles!), and of course the bottom level with a hidden cache of gems.


: When you kick a box/chest, and something shatters, is that always just a
: gem, or could it be valuable things too??

	Only glass shatters when kicked / being inside a container which
 is kicked. There are several items made of glass, namely all potions,
 worthless pieces of glass, glass wands, and crystal plate mails
 (surprise?!)


